WEBVTT

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.500
Who are you?

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.220
N-No one suspicious or anything.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:31.910
Uh, you look suspicious to me!

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.190
What are you doing?

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:33.770
Are you a thief?

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:34.740
No!

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.510
I am

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:39.270
a superhero.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.980
<b>Debut of Samurai Flamenco!</b>

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:20.610
<b></b>

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.890
Totsuka-san...

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:23.700
Huh?

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:26.990
Would you say Kamen Rider operates 
his motorcycle without a helmet?

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.290
Hmm...

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:32.710
Does the mask count as a helmet in this case?

00:02:32.710 --> 00:02:37.890
If it doesn't, he's a law-breaking superhero.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:41.150
Goto, it's just a TV show.

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:41.950
Yeah.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.410
Do your job.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:46.140
Arrest the criminals that 
don't follow society's rules,

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.250
while protecting innocent 
citizens and their wallets.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:51.150
Yeah.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.530
<b>Sub: Missing! 

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.260
You did...

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.540
<b>Sub: Re: Re: Missing! 

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:32.170
You missed...

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.940
That was pathetic!

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:34.570
Who's up next?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.540
Here, let me try.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:39.900
Do you have a rewards card?

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.740
Thank you very much.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.570
Will the second person in line step up?

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:47.390
One pack of Mild Sevens.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:48.910
Yes.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:52.000
Um, that'll be 410 yen.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.670
Huh? Oh, where's my wallet...

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.270
Who are you?

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.780
N-No one suspicious or anything.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.780
Uh, you look suspicious to me!

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.020
What are you doing?

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:25.880
Are you a thief?

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:26.780
No!

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.260
I am

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.910
a superhero.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.460
An exhibitionist?

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.660
No, I'm not!

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:35.680
Don't move!

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.880
You're under arrest!

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:39.910
A-Are you a cop?

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:41.670
Please listen... I can explain.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.450
I told you not to move!

00:04:43.450 --> 00:04:45.250
Hear me out!

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.200
W-Water!

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.190
Water... Water!

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.910
That's my suit...

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:09.330
Oh, really...

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:11.820
You set it on fire.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:17.010
At least the liquid was clear.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:18.460
Yes, I suppose.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:21.800
Uh, would you mind stopping by my place first?

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:23.480
This is uncomfortable.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:42.970
Please have a seat.

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:43.900
I'll go get changed.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.030
I live alone, so make yourself at home.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.530
He lives here by himself?

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.090
A fate worse than death.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.710
"Hazama Masayoshi"?

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:11.330
Yes.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.350
You're a model?

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:15.760
Yeah...

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.980
You can have this back.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.230
<b>Garbage Bag</b>

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:20.230
No, thanks!

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:23.610
So what were you doing out there?

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:26.420
I was fighting evil...

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.110
Evil?

00:06:28.690 --> 00:06:30.360
A drunk man was jaywalking,

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:34.120
and smoking in a non-smoking zone.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.240
<b>Shibiru City</b>

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.720
I was going to let him off with a warning,

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:38.810
but he attacked me.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:39.620
The hell?!

00:06:40.930 --> 00:06:43.130
That's when my suit got torn.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:45.080
Hold on...

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:47.460
So the evil you were fighting was a drunk?

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:48.240
Yes.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.510
You got in a fight with a drunk?

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:52.240
He was jaywalking...

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:53.760
And smoking on the street!

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:57.060
I was confronting an evil villain 
threatening our city's safety!

00:06:57.530 --> 00:06:59.260
You're getting a little carried away...

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:01.690
Plenty of people jaywalk and smoke.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.640
And if you give them a warning, they ignore you.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:05.590
You should just ignore them...

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:07.780
The world's more peaceful that way.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.030
But then, there's no justice!

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:15.450
<i>Change Sunshine!</i>

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:20.780
Huh? What?

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:25.920
<i>I shall punish you.</i>

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:28.760
Harakiri Sunshine?

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:35.100
<i>Harakiri Cut!</i>

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:43.810
That's an ancient show.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:45.150
It isn't ancient...

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.000
It's still very relevant.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:48.860
Right now, the world needs heroes!

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:53.160
I grew up watching heroes in action.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:55.280
And I'm not the only one...

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:58.870
Their heroics inspired every boy in Japan.

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:02.160
But when they grew up, 
they found other interests...

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:06.320
Like soccer, video games, music, 
motorcycles, and girls.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:10.380
They stopped dreaming of becoming heroes 
to pursue those other interests.

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:12.580
But I was different.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:14.020
I wanted to become a hero.

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:17.400
I studied hard and worked out, so I could do it.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.930
But one day, my teacher told me the truth.

00:08:21.280 --> 00:08:23.390
There wasn't any job market for superheroes.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.140
It turned my world upside-down.

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.780
Um, Hazama-kun?

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:32.140
Call me "Masayoshi."

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:35.750
I prefer that name because it uses 
the characters for "justice."

00:08:35.750 --> 00:08:37.210
<i>This kid's too much...</i>

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.290
Masayoshi-kun, how old were you?

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:42.250
I was a second-year in middle school.

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:44.430
And that whole time, you never realized

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:46.960
that superheroes on TV shows were fictional?

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.530
I noticed that they weren't real...

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:52.260
But you know how people 
give Christmas presents,

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.510
even though they don't believe in Santa Claus?

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:58.150
I thought there was some kind of workaround.

00:08:58.150 --> 00:08:59.030
There isn't!

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:01.100
And your example is completely unrelated!

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.540
Haven't heard that in a while...

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.440
My teacher said the same thing.

00:09:05.950 --> 00:09:07.770
<i>Yeah, I want to smack him hard!</i>

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:11.280
My teacher told me to 
consider other career tracks.

00:09:11.910 --> 00:09:14.740
But I never gave up on becoming a hero.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:20.470
Well, you could have become a policeman 
or an attorney and fought evil that way.

00:09:20.930 --> 00:09:23.000
But I wanted to be a hero.

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:27.970
You're asking me to settle for curry udon 
when I really want curry rice!

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:29.970
What's the problem?

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.390
You're still getting curry.

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:35.800
That just highlights the difference 
between udon and rice!

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:41.260
Now you've made me crave curry.

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:44.020
I can whip some up.

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:55.940
Did you assemble this collection?

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:59.660
No, I inherited half of them from my grandpa.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.580
<b>Samurai Flamenco</b>

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:04.580
"Curry is the soul of a hero!"

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.080
<b>Brass Rangers 
Ensemble Curry</b>

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.130
After graduating from high school, 
I was scouted by my current agency,

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:12.840
and I became a model.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.800
I didn't have any skills to speak of,

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.750
so I was fortunate to land this job.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:26.390
I was surrounded by staff that 
helped pull everything together.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:28.600
But at the same time,

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:32.520
my desire to become a hero 
only grew stronger each day.

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:35.400
That was when it hit me.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:37.750
Without taking any action,

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:40.710
it wasn't like I'd be kidnapped 
and turned into a cyborg,

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:43.120
or wake up one day with superpowers...

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:45.800
Given that, I was going to 
have to do it the hard way!

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:51.410
I asked a fashion designer 
I know to make me this suit.

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:52.540
And that was the birth of...

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.480
"Samurai Flamenco"?

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:56.670
Yes!

00:10:56.980 --> 00:10:58.530
And where are the bad guys?

00:10:58.530 --> 00:10:59.930
What are you fighting?

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:03.220
There aren't really any mutants or monsters.

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:04.330
Exactly!

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:09.630
Without bad guys, a hero has nothing to do.

00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:12.350
That's why I'm trying a different approach.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.560
I'm a brand-new hero.

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:18.570
So I should start with small-time criminals.

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:20.370
My debut will come against

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:23.760
a petty offender who wouldn't even 
get a mention in the papers...

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.910
After I've accumulated experience 
and leveled up as a superhero,

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.590
I can move onto bigger fish.

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:33.250
Hold on... That sounds like you're 
settling for curry udon.

00:11:33.570 --> 00:11:34.080
Huh?

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:39.150
You'll be fighting low-life street thugs... 
The same ones we cops deal with every day.

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:44.650
Except that a businessman beat you up 
before you even located a thug.

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:47.630
It was my first time in an actual fight...

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:52.150
Honestly, you're settling for 
even less than curry udon.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:53.270
We're talking artificial curry.

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:58.270
Sorry, I need a smoke.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.590
In this city, there is evil

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:08.990
that hides in the shadows, 
unseen by the public.

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:13.460
And where there is evil, there is suffering.

00:12:14.050 --> 00:12:16.740
Smokers that follow the rules 
are discriminated against,

00:12:16.740 --> 00:12:18.410
thanks to a few lawbreakers.

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:20.920
Jaywalkers cause accidents.

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:23.480
The crimes may be small,

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:26.470
but they won't end until someone stops them.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:30.930
I admit that I'm powerless at the moment,

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.140
so I'm trying to take it slow.

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:36.540
I'll turn myself in and explain everything,

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:40.840
so please don't smoke in non-smoking areas.

00:12:43.340 --> 00:12:45.740
I understand where you're coming from.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.450
Did you punch the other guy?

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:50.130
No, it was a one-sided beating.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:55.500
Your clothes were on fire, so I guess you 
didn't choose to expose yourself.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:56.420
No...

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.670
I'll let you go this one time.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.630
Thank you so much, officer!

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:04.760
Call me Goto... I'm Goto Hidenori.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.880
Don't do anything like this again.

00:13:06.880 --> 00:13:08.090
Okay!

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:12.460
Someone might have reported you, 
so give me your phone number.

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:13.300
Right!

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:19.980
A questionnaire for the show you'll be on.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:21.820
You have two days to complete it.

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:25.190
Do I have to fill this out?

00:13:25.190 --> 00:13:28.700
Masayoshi-kun, you can't sing or act,

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:31.200
so variety shows are the only 
way you'll get screen time.

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:34.060
But I'm not good at talking.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.500
Then you should train harder.

00:13:36.060 --> 00:13:37.370
Train harder?

00:13:38.540 --> 00:13:40.590
This is Ishihara from Caesar Pro.

00:13:41.190 --> 00:13:43.170
Oh, thank you very much.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:43.170
Train harder...

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.210
Should have asked for an autograph...

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:49.910
Goto, you have a visitor.

00:13:50.780 --> 00:13:51.850
Goto-san!

00:13:52.550 --> 00:13:54.180
Eh? Why are you here?

00:13:54.770 --> 00:13:58.310
I had your shirt dry-cleaned, 
so I wanted to drop it off.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:13:59.060
Eh?

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:00.850
Ah, I see...

00:14:00.850 --> 00:14:02.780
Thanks for taking the trouble... Goodbye!

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:05.080
How did you know where to find me?!

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:08.090
I checked every station in the area.

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:09.280
Don't show up without warning...

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:10.230
Give a call first!

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:11.120
I'm sorry.

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:13.080
I wanted to thank you for 
your advice yesterday.

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:15.540
O-Oh...

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:23.760
Goto-san, are you busy tomorrow night?

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:25.630
<i>Wait, Sunset!</i>

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:28.560
<i>Why must we fight?</i>

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:27.220
Huh?

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:28.550
Look!

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:30.930
The design's slightly different for the movie!

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:33.250
<i>Did I make a really good impression?</i>

00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:36.640
Oh... The next part with Sunshine 
will move you to tears!

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:36.970
<i>Are you sure about this?</i>

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:39.900
<i>Why did you become a hero?</i>

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:40.560
An e-mail.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:41.730
From your girlfriend?

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.430
<i>What have you been working for?</i>

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:42.710
Yeah.

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:44.380
<i>What do you live for?</i>

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.900
Well, you could invite her here.

00:14:44.850 --> 00:14:46.680
<i>Each step I take is scary.</i>

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.390
No need for that.

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:49.030
<i>Because it may be the one 
that leads to my death.</i>

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:49.030
We're in a long-distance relationship.

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:53.650
Sunshine really does have 
some tearjerker moments.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.790
The ones who haven't seen it don't 
know what they're missing.

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:02.640
Does your agency know about this...

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:03.880
hobby of yours?

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:07.560
No, Ishihara-san would have a fit if she knew.

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:09.720
She really scares me.

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:11.930
You're the only one who knows my secret!

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:14.110
That just sounded creepy.

00:15:14.110 --> 00:15:15.880
I didn't want to know your secret!

00:15:16.330 --> 00:15:18.050
I'm only giving you one pass.

00:15:18.050 --> 00:15:19.020
Don't try it again!

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:20.540
Got it.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:30.360
Totsuka-san, excuse me for a moment.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:35.260
Yes?

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:37.200
Goto-san! I really screwed up!

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:42.620
I found a spare suit in a different 
color, so I wanted to try it out.

00:15:42.620 --> 00:15:43.940
Ah, I see...

00:15:43.940 --> 00:15:45.630
You're a complete idiot!

00:15:47.730 --> 00:15:48.830
You really suck.

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:50.300
It won't go in.

00:15:49.270 --> 00:15:52.640
I told some middle schoolers to go home.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:56.970
And now, they're targeting me.

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:00.460
I told you to stop playing vigilante!

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:03.350
Well? What's the situation?

00:16:03.950 --> 00:16:06.510
Right now, I'm running from them...

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:08.050
I'll bail you out!

00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:08.850
Where are you?

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:11.400
Right! Uh...

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:14.140
<i>Are you sure about this?</i>

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:16.120
Harakiri Sunshine?

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.520
Wait, wh-what?

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:20.080
<i>Why did you become a hero?</i>

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.080
<i>What have you been working for?</i>

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:23.850
<i>What do you live for?</i>

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.170
<i>Each step I take is scary.</i>

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:29.970
<i>Because it may be the one 
that leads to my death.</i>

00:16:30.400 --> 00:16:34.110
<i>However, thinking about what will 
happen if I run away is scarier.</i>

00:16:34.400 --> 00:16:38.040
<i>So no matter the foe, I never back down.</i>

00:16:38.680 --> 00:16:40.740
<i>That is the Sunshine way.</i>

00:16:41.990 --> 00:16:44.140
Sunshine!

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:45.810
H-Hey, Masayoshi!

00:16:45.810 --> 00:16:47.210
I'm sorry, Goto-san...

00:16:47.210 --> 00:16:49.130
I've screwed up!

00:16:49.130 --> 00:16:50.350
Just tell me where you are...

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:51.190
Hurry up!

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:54.110
That's why I'm going to see what else I can do!

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:54.950
Huh?

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:58.660
That idiot!

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:01.210
Sorry! Someone called in an incident!

00:17:01.210 --> 00:17:01.920
Huh?

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:02.850
Hey!

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:09.250
<i>There aren't many public phones left...</i>

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:12.480
Where'd you go, tough guy?

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:14.210
Aren't you going to play with us?

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:15.200
You're too heavy.

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:21.400
I've come to nip you kids in the bud,

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:23.770
before you bloom into flowers of evil!

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:24.730
They call me

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:26.690
Samurai Flamenco!

00:17:32.990 --> 00:17:35.300
What's with the threads? Some kind of freak?

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:35.300
Ready to die?!

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:37.420
Go home...

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:39.040
You go home!

00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:40.990
You filming this?

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:42.630
Yep.

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:44.870
We're gonna slay this freak.

00:17:44.870 --> 00:17:46.530
You must stop disrupting traffic...

00:17:46.530 --> 00:17:48.170
Stop making noise in public places!

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:51.470
Stop walking around in the middle of the night!

00:17:51.680 --> 00:17:53.800
Is this freak trying to lecture us?

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:54.870
Who the hell are you?

00:17:57.230 --> 00:17:58.210
Did you get that?

00:17:58.210 --> 00:17:59.570
You bet!

00:17:58.670 --> 00:18:00.470
We're all friends here...

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:02.660
Friends who wanted to get together and chat.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:04.210
Were we bothering anyone?

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:06.220
You should leave us alone!

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:07.900
Yikes, that looked bad...

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:10.310
Take it off.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:17.450
You kids...

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:18.720
Eh, what's this?

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:23.520
You kids must be enjoying yourselves...

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:27.190
You believe that you're special...

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.480
That you can do anything.

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:33.920
The sky's the limit...

00:18:34.390 --> 00:18:36.240
All you care about is

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:39.500
hanging out with friends and fooling around...

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:43.850
But your parents and other 
adults don't understand.

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:47.520
That's your current mindset...

00:18:48.220 --> 00:18:53.860
You think no one cares if you 
act like you own the world!

00:18:55.540 --> 00:18:57.280
But you're wrong.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:18:58.970
People do mind.

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:00.820
You're a damned nuisance.

00:19:01.520 --> 00:19:04.640
But no one says anything because 
they don't want any trouble.

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:07.510
They're scared, so they keep their mouths shut.

00:19:08.130 --> 00:19:11.750
They don't step in because they 
don't care what happens to you.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:17.200
As they sneer at you and keep their 
mouths shut, those adults think,

00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:20.790
"Those kids won't amount to anything in life."

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:24.070
But here's what I think.

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:27.730
If we don't get you kids home, 
nothing will change...

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:30.390
The city won't change, society won't,

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:32.290
our future won't, adults won't...

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:34.650
You won't change... I won't change.

00:19:35.390 --> 00:19:38.110
That's why I'm here to tell you 
you're being a nuisance!

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:39.640
Don't block the streets.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:41.740
Don't shout in the middle 
of the night. Go home!

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.160
If you want to be a bother, annoy your parents!

00:19:44.670 --> 00:19:46.990
They're the only people in the world

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.950
who absolutely have to

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:50.580
care about you!

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:05.300
Lame.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:07.070
Hey! What are you doing?

00:20:07.070 --> 00:20:07.800
Let's go.

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:09.550
Run for it!

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:10.880
Don't ditch me!

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:12.270
Oh, crap!

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:13.190
Sawada!

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:15.900
What are you trying to do, idiot?!

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:21.610
Goto-san... Would you consider that curry rice?

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:26.130
Curry rice with a kick.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:31.660
So why weren't you carrying your cell phone?

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.030
When I put my cell phone in this suit's pocket,

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:36.670
it's really visible...

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:39.000
I'll have to modify it.

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:42.010
You haven't given up yet?

00:22:31.310 --> 00:22:33.080
<i>You're being a nuisance!</i>

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:34.120
<i>Don't block the streets.</i>

00:22:33.450 --> 00:22:34.860
Who is this guy?

00:22:34.120 --> 00:22:36.140
<i>Don't shout in the middle 
of the night. Go home!</i>

00:22:34.860 --> 00:22:38.040
Well, I guess he's supposed to be a superhero.

00:22:36.140 --> 00:22:38.040
<i>If you want to be a bother, annoy your parents!</i>

00:22:40.440 --> 00:22:42.130
The light's red, sir!

00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:43.630
Ah, hey!

00:22:45.070 --> 00:22:45.850
Yes?

00:22:45.850 --> 00:22:48.010
Goto-san! I screwed up!

00:22:48.010 --> 00:22:50.010
<b>My Umbrella Is Missing</b>

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:55.010
<b>Watch again next week, gyasu!</b>
